      <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:Package" xmi:id="cdi" xmi:uuid="fe399a52-1d47-5b05-812a-b021581619b1">
        <name>DDICDI</name>
        <URI>https://w3id.org/cdif/cdi/xmi/</URI>
        <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:Class" xmi:id="cdi.CategoryStatistics" xmi:uuid="c627c172-8254-5dd4-bf9e-adf15cd17ef9">
          <name>CategoryStatistics</name>
          <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="cdi.CategoryStatistics.comment" xmi:uuid="4291c590-99d4-59b9-b96a-69370259abb8">
            <body>**CDIF**

Definition
==========

Statistics for a specific Category of an instance variable within a data set. Maps a **Statistic** value object to a category concept. The Statistic value object represents a single computed value (mean, count, median, etc.), with optional computationBase and typeOfNumericValue.

**Original (DDICDI)**

*Definition:* Statistics related to a specific category of an instance variable within a data set.

*Examples:* The percentage of females from a demographic data set.

`Specification item reference &lt;https://ddi-cdi.github.io/m2t-ng/DDI-CDI_1-1beta/field-level-documentation/DDICDILibrary/Classes/DataDescription/CategoryStatistics.html&gt;`__</body>
            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.CategoryStatistics"/>
          </ownedComment>
          <ownedAttribute xmi:type="uml:Property" xmi:id="cdi.CategoryStatistics.statistic" xmi:uuid="a77782d6-4822-59da-bace-6126d1720260">
            <name>statistic</name>
            <type xmi:idref="common.ObjectReference"/>
            <lowerValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger" xmi:id="cdi.CategoryStatistics.statistic.lower" xmi:uuid="7cd82103-41d8-5911-876d-e1f7674a2b2a">
              <value>0</value>
            </lowerValue>
            <upperValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural" xmi:id="cdi.CategoryStatistics.statistic.upper" xmi:uuid="95b8f990-5647-58f5-8daa-d629ef0c7f15">
              <value>1</value>
            </upperValue>
            <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="cdi.CategoryStatistics.statistic.comment" xmi:uuid="c4bf0a9f-3696-546e-aa58-e55ecafaca5b">
              <body>**CDIF**

Definition
==========

Per-category Statistic value objects. In line Statistic instance or object reference.

**Original (DDICDI)**

`Specification item reference &lt;https://ddi-cdi.github.io/m2t-ng/DDI-CDI_1-1beta/field-level-documentation/DDICDILibrary/Classes/DataDescription/CategoryStatistics.html&gt;`__</body>
              <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.CategoryStatistics.statistic"/>
            </ownedComment>
          </ownedAttribute>
          <ownedAttribute xmi:type="uml:Property" xmi:id="cdi.CategoryStatistics.CategoryStatistics_for_Concept" xmi:uuid="d778ee70-605b-524b-8c6d-f092baeed6fd">
            <lowerValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger" xmi:id="cdi.CategoryStatistics.CategoryStatistics_for_Concept.lower" xmi:uuid="596ec9d4-1c01-5c7b-9c50-212771cc0e30">
              <value>0</value>
            </lowerValue>
            <upperValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural" xmi:id="cdi.CategoryStatistics.CategoryStatistics_for_Concept.upper" xmi:uuid="951ea893-0611-5fa6-b82c-ef731d7377d3">
              <value>1</value>
            </upperValue>
            <association xmi:idref="assoc.CategoryStatistics_for_Concept"/>
            <type xmi:idref="skos.Concept"/>
            <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="cdi.CategoryStatistics.CategoryStatistics_for_Concept.comment" xmi:uuid="f5c8fb2e-1606-5b10-9461-c9363cd9c344">
              <body>**CDIF**

Definition
==========

The Category this CategoryStatistics is for (inline CDIF Concept or an object reference).

**Original (DDICDI)**

`Specification item reference &lt;https://ddi-cdi.github.io/m2t-ng/DDI-CDI_1-1beta/field-level-documentation/DDICDILibrary/Classes/DataDescription/CategoryStatistics.html&gt;`__</body>
              <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.CategoryStatistics.CategoryStatistics_for_Concept"/>
            </ownedComment>
          </ownedAttribute>
          <ownedAttribute xmi:type="uml:Property" xmi:id="cdi.CategoryStatistics.CategoryStatistics_typeOfStatistic_Concept" xmi:uuid="0962ff18-0439-584f-adec-2d9895f936ff">
            <lowerValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger" xmi:id="cdi.CategoryStatistics.CategoryStatistics_typeOfStatistic_Concept.lower" xmi:uuid="7f82c7fe-5e18-564b-914c-3bc14612ef74">
              <value>0</value>
            </lowerValue>
            <upperValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural" xmi:id="cdi.CategoryStatistics.CategoryStatistics_typeOfStatistic_Concept.upper" xmi:uuid="d8486212-d10d-5a3b-ad8c-2df5c82758a2">
              <value>1</value>
            </upperValue>
            <association xmi:idref="assoc.CategoryStatistics_typeOfStatistic_Concept"/>
            <type xmi:idref="skos.Concept"/>
            <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="cdi.CategoryStatistics.CategoryStatistics_typeOfStatistic_Concept.comment" xmi:uuid="c92a55ec-ebcb-538f-b8cd-b8d3e3f76116">
              <body>**CDIF**

Definition
==========

Controlled-vocabulary entry naming the kind of statistic. Inline CDIF concept or object reference

**Original (DDICDI)**

`Specification item reference &lt;https://ddi-cdi.github.io/m2t-ng/DDI-CDI_1-1beta/field-level-documentation/DDICDILibrary/Classes/DataDescription/CategoryStatistics.html&gt;`__</body>
              <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.CategoryStatistics.CategoryStatistics_typeOfStatistic_Concept"/>
            </ownedComment>
          </ownedAttribute>
          <ownedAttribute xmi:type="uml:Property" xmi:id="cdi.CategoryStatistics.CategoryStatistics_hasWeight_InstanceVariable" xmi:uuid="1ce434f7-f04d-5ea7-944b-c8b355748426">
            <lowerValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger" xmi:id="cdi.CategoryStatistics.CategoryStatistics_hasWeight_InstanceVariable.lower" xmi:uuid="bbfc977f-fcf1-53ad-b2c9-d7b06b11606b">
              <value>0</value>
            </lowerValue>
            <upperValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural" xmi:id="cdi.CategoryStatistics.CategoryStatistics_hasWeight_InstanceVariable.upper" xmi:uuid="6686fbd2-376b-5cd7-b2f7-e2ab69071c24">
              <value>1</value>
            </upperValue>
            <association xmi:idref="assoc.CategoryStatistics_hasWeight_InstanceVariable"/>
            <type xmi:idref="cdif.InstanceVariable"/>
            <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="cdi.CategoryStatistics.CategoryStatistics_hasWeight_InstanceVariable.comment" xmi:uuid="51ea2e39-d2da-5220-9c41-19018231caf0">
              <body>**CDIF**

Definition
==========

The InstanceVariable whose values were used as weights (an @id-reference).

**Original (DDICDI)**

`Specification item reference &lt;https://ddi-cdi.github.io/m2t-ng/DDI-CDI_1-1beta/field-level-documentation/DDICDILibrary/Classes/DataDescription/CategoryStatistics.html&gt;`__</body>
              <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.CategoryStatistics.CategoryStatistics_hasWeight_InstanceVariable"/>
            </ownedComment>
          </ownedAttribute>
        </packagedElement>
        <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:Class" xmi:id="cdi.DataStructure" xmi:uuid="f75dffb6-4d70-5d71-9881-972acd00135c">
          <name>DataStructure</name>
          <isAbstract>true</isAbstract>
          <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="cdi.DataStructure.comment" xmi:uuid="6ea2458d-74a1-5058-af10-2b2a09cec029">
            <body>**CDIF**

Definition
==========

Abstract base for ``cdi:DimensionalDataStructure``, ``cdi:LongDataStructure``, and ``cdi:WideDataStructure``. Instances are always typed as one of those subtypes; this class is never instantiated directly. It carries the common properties listed below; the subtypes constrain which ``DataStructureComponent`` kinds may appear in ``cdi:has_DataStructureComponent``.

**Original (DDICDI)**

*Definition:* Data organization based on reusable data structure components.

`Specification item reference &lt;https://ddi-cdi.github.io/m2t-ng/DDI-CDI_1-1beta/field-level-documentation/DDICDILibrary/Classes/DataDescription/DataStructure.html&gt;`__</body>
            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdi.DataStructure"/>
          </ownedComment>
          <ownedAttribute xmi:type="uml:Property" xmi:id="cdi.DataStructure.DataStructure_has_DataStructureComponent" xmi:uuid="7f976b15-4cae-5776-b683-c6375f298df2">
            <lowerValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger" xmi:id="cdi.DataStructure.DataStructure_has_DataStructureComponent.lower" xmi:uuid="2b29c6a9-4e79-5388-9d4b-0cc6dd90af05">
              <value>1</value>
            </lowerValue>
            <upperValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural" xmi:id="cdi.DataStructure.DataStructure_has_DataStructureComponent.upper" xmi:uuid="d0ededd3-66a6-5454-9e93-478df6d42acb">
              <value>*</value>
            </upperValue>
            <association xmi:idref="assoc.DataStructure_has_DataStructureComponent"/>
            <type xmi:idref="cdif.DataStructureComponent"/>
            <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="cdi.DataStructure.DataStructure_has_DataStructureComponent.comment" xmi:uuid="64568088-2285-57dd-9c59-14b3e3445eea">
              <body>**CDIF**

Definition
==========

The components that make up the data structure. The valid component subtypes depend on the concrete DataStructure subtype — see each subtype below.

**Original (DDICDI)**

