          <ownedAttribute xmi:type="uml:Property" xmi:id="cdif.Dataset.Dataset_hasPrimaryKey" xmi:uuid="87caa527-b61e-5a9d-bb32-497b924b6c82">
            <lowerValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger" xmi:id="cdif.Dataset.Dataset_hasPrimaryKey.lower" xmi:uuid="b2f88eda-a0e3-5b09-b4df-79817cfdd05e">
              <value>0</value>
            </lowerValue>
            <upperValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural" xmi:id="cdif.Dataset.Dataset_hasPrimaryKey.upper" xmi:uuid="9b592b06-a062-55b1-8092-0dba96570ac5">
              <value>1</value>
            </upperValue>
            <association xmi:idref="assoc.Dataset_hasPrimaryKey"/>
            <type xmi:idref="cdif.PrimaryKey"/>
            <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="cdif.Dataset.Dataset_hasPrimaryKey.comment" xmi:uuid="07a2b9d3-2738-5ba1-8d2a-7236288fef3e">
              <body>**CDIF**

Definition
==========

the value is an object reference to a cdif:Key, or an inline cdif:Key. The cdif:Key is  an ordered set of cdi:InstanceVariables that uniquely identify a data instance. Each variable's position in the key is has a cdi:value integer that positions the variable in an ordered key. The cdif:Key object is a profile of the canonical DDI-CDI PrimaryKey structure matching. In the DataStructure profile, key (primary and foreign) are indexed by RepresentedVariable, not InstanceVariable.</body>
              <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdif.Dataset.Dataset_hasPrimaryKey"/>
            </ownedComment>
          </ownedAttribute>
          <ownedAttribute xmi:type="uml:Property" xmi:id="cdif.Dataset.Dataset_schema_variableMeasured_InstanceVariable" xmi:uuid="b7b25d94-0352-561a-876a-312534dfeee7">
            <lowerValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger" xmi:id="cdif.Dataset.Dataset_schema_variableMeasured_InstanceVariable.lower" xmi:uuid="066bf2d2-5876-5b0e-9e37-c9814d8cfd1c">
              <value>0</value>
            </lowerValue>
            <upperValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural" xmi:id="cdif.Dataset.Dataset_schema_variableMeasured_InstanceVariable.upper" xmi:uuid="20c9da49-057a-5475-92a1-0745867ec589">
              <value>1</value>
            </upperValue>
            <association xmi:idref="assoc.Dataset_schema_variableMeasured_InstanceVariable"/>
            <type xmi:idref="cdif.InstanceVariable"/>
            <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="cdif.Dataset.Dataset_schema_variableMeasured_InstanceVariable.comment" xmi:uuid="08bd2a0c-cd53-539a-84b1-294fa7fb4888">
              <body>**CDIF**

Definition
==========

The DataDescription profile add **cdi:InstanceVariable** as a type for the schema:variableMeasured property. If the DataDescription profile is composed with the Discovery profile, the schema @type will include both schema:PropertyValue and cdi:InstanceVariable.

**Original (Schema)**

*Definition:* The variableMeasured property can indicate (repeated as necessary) the  variables that are measured in some dataset, either described as text or as pairs of identifier and description using PropertyValue, or more explicitly as a StatisticalVariable.

`Specification item reference &lt;https://schema.org/variableMeasured&gt;`__</body>
              <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdif.Dataset.Dataset_schema_variableMeasured_InstanceVariable"/>
            </ownedComment>
          </ownedAttribute>
