        <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:Class" xmi:id="cdif.TextMapping" xmi:uuid="1976b5b9-41be-5045-bdc9-2a9b2545da92">
          <name>TextMapping</name>
          <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="cdif.TextMapping.comment" xmi:uuid="dfbb4c81-528a-5b70-afad-624591d800e2">
            <body>**CDIF**

Definition
==========

Physical mapping for a variable in a delimited or fixed-width text dataset. Extends cdifPhysicalMapping with text-format properties (column width and number formatting).</body>
            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdif.TextMapping"/>
          </ownedComment>
          <generalization xmi:type="uml:Generalization" xmi:id="cdif.TextMapping.gen.AbstractMapping" xmi:uuid="8ca738be-b81a-5f9d-836c-0d39b4490e7e">
            <general xmi:idref="cdif.AbstractMapping"/>
          </generalization>
          <ownedAttribute xmi:type="uml:Property" xmi:id="cdif.TextMapping.displayLabel" xmi:uuid="c4d16d2e-5f39-5022-b73f-a09e0b028e6b">
            <name>displayLabel</name>
            <type xmi:type="uml:PrimitiveType" href="http://www.omg.org/spec/UML/20161101/PrimitiveTypes.xmi#String"/>
            <lowerValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger" xmi:id="cdif.TextMapping.displayLabel.lower" xmi:uuid="a7690691-b549-556a-9572-a46e663131f7">
              <value>0</value>
            </lowerValue>
            <upperValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural" xmi:id="cdif.TextMapping.displayLabel.upper" xmi:uuid="ef00a32f-5539-5371-82b5-f6ad9dee53ce">
              <value>1</value>
            </upperValue>
            <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="cdif.TextMapping.displayLabel.comment" xmi:uuid="3eb2136f-f11f-560f-8d45-4ca37988b651">
              <body>**CDIF**

Definition
==========

Human-readable text string for display. CDIF simplification (plain string) of DDI-CDI TextMapping.displayLabel, whose model type is LabelForDisplay. Per the cdi/cdif namespace policy a structured-string type simplified to a plain string is in the cdif namespace.</body>
              <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdif.TextMapping.displayLabel"/>
            </ownedComment>
          </ownedAttribute>
          <ownedAttribute xmi:type="uml:Property" xmi:id="cdif.TextMapping.TextMapping_cdi_length_TextMapping" xmi:uuid="ff03b0c8-2616-5053-9277-f093df921188">
            <lowerValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger" xmi:id="cdif.TextMapping.TextMapping_cdi_length_TextMapping.lower" xmi:uuid="72757fc1-0a69-5802-a4e4-1d07fae9f7fc">
              <value>0</value>
            </lowerValue>
            <upperValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural" xmi:id="cdif.TextMapping.TextMapping_cdi_length_TextMapping.upper" xmi:uuid="cdac6dd8-cd8f-545e-a154-b1052f7a19dd">
              <value>1</value>
            </upperValue>
            <association xmi:idref="assoc.TextMapping_cdi_length_TextMapping"/>
            <type xmi:idref="cdif.TextMapping"/>
            <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="cdif.TextMapping.TextMapping_cdi_length_TextMapping.comment" xmi:uuid="1a436856-a1e1-5032-807c-0f00cdaaa94d">
              <body>**CDIF**

Definition
==========

The column width if the tabular text is fixed width (TextMapping.length). type: integer

**Original (DDICDI)**

*Definition:* Length in characters of the physical representation of the value. From the W3C Recommendation "Metadata Vocabulary for Tabular Data" (https://www.w3.org/TR/tabular-metadata/)  5.11.2 "length: A numeric atomic property that contains a single integer that is the exact length of the value. The value of this property becomes the length annotation for the described datatype. See Length Constraints in [tabular-data-model] for details." Corresponds to DDI2.5 var/location/width and DDI 3.2 PhysicalLocation/Width.

`Specification item reference &lt;https://ddi-cdi.github.io/m2t-ng/DDI-CDI_1-1beta/field-level-documentation/DDICDILibrary/Classes/FormatDescription/TextMapping.html&gt;`__</body>
              <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdif.TextMapping.TextMapping_cdi_length_TextMapping"/>
            </ownedComment>
          </ownedAttribute>
          <ownedAttribute xmi:type="uml:Property" xmi:id="cdif.TextMapping.TextMapping_cdi_defaultDecimalSeparator_TextMapping" xmi:uuid="51763b6d-0431-5a1b-91f8-872390041022">
            <lowerValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger" xmi:id="cdif.TextMapping.TextMapping_cdi_defaultDecimalSeparator_TextMapping.lower" xmi:uuid="5709bf07-4eb1-54b3-a7a8-34818f59274e">
              <value>0</value>
            </lowerValue>
            <upperValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural" xmi:id="cdif.TextMapping.TextMapping_cdi_defaultDecimalSeparator_TextMapping.upper" xmi:uuid="17c3f5dd-123a-598c-a99d-c2ad1eac1ee7">
              <value>1</value>
            </upperValue>
            <association xmi:idref="assoc.TextMapping_cdi_defaultDecimalSeparator_TextMapping"/>
            <type xmi:idref="cdif.TextMapping"/>
            <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="cdif.TextMapping.TextMapping_cdi_defaultDecimalSeparator_TextMapping.comment" xmi:uuid="3e23f017-812e-5f21-834d-82cfc0f626c2">
              <body>**CDIF**

Definition
==========

Decimal separator used when not otherwise specified (TextMapping.defaultDecimalSeparator). type: string

**Original (DDICDI)**

*Definition:* Default value is "." (period). The character separating the integer part from the fractional part of a decimal or real number. From the W3C Recommendation "Metadata Vocabulary for Tabular Data" (https://www.w3.org/TR/tabular-metadata/) 6.4.2: "decimalChar: A string whose value is used to represent a decimal point within the number. If the supplied value is not a string, implementations MUST issue a warning and proceed as if the property had not been specified."

`Specification item reference &lt;https://ddi-cdi.github.io/m2t-ng/DDI-CDI_1-1beta/field-level-documentation/DDICDILibrary/Classes/FormatDescription/TextMapping.html&gt;`__</body>
              <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdif.TextMapping.TextMapping_cdi_defaultDecimalSeparator_TextMapping"/>
            </ownedComment>
          </ownedAttribute>
          <ownedAttribute xmi:type="uml:Property" xmi:id="cdif.TextMapping.TextMapping_cdi_defaultDigitGroupSeparator_TextMapping" xmi:uuid="c6c2e28d-d363-5225-9a3b-615955dd4c5d">
            <lowerValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger" xmi:id="cdif.TextMapping.TextMapping_cdi_defaultDigitGroupSeparator_TextMapping.lower" xmi:uuid="7f61321c-942f-5e57-a084-30311c32cf87">
              <value>0</value>
            </lowerValue>
            <upperValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural" xmi:id="cdif.TextMapping.TextMapping_cdi_defaultDigitGroupSeparator_TextMapping.upper" xmi:uuid="fd7b773c-d58c-55e5-b68d-3f8ed33db827">
              <value>1</value>
            </upperValue>
            <association xmi:idref="assoc.TextMapping_cdi_defaultDigitGroupSeparator_TextMapping"/>
            <type xmi:idref="cdif.TextMapping"/>
            <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="cdif.TextMapping.TextMapping_cdi_defaultDigitGroupSeparator_TextMapping.comment" xmi:uuid="9bda6ccf-42fa-521b-a0a3-7cc910c6ee2b">
              <body>**CDIF**

Definition
==========

Digit-group (thousands) separator (TextMapping.defaultDigitGroupSeparator). type: string

**Original (DDICDI)**

*Definition:* Default value is null. A character separating groups of digits (for readability). In W3C part of the datatype format From https://www.w3.org/TR/tabular-metadata/ tabular 6.4.2 groupChar: "A string whose value is used to group digits within the number. If the supplied value is not a string, implementations MUST issue a warning and proceed as if the property had not been specified."

`Specification item reference &lt;https://ddi-cdi.github.io/m2t-ng/DDI-CDI_1-1beta/field-level-documentation/DDICDILibrary/Classes/FormatDescription/TextMapping.html&gt;`__</body>
              <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdif.TextMapping.TextMapping_cdi_defaultDigitGroupSeparator_TextMapping"/>
            </ownedComment>
          </ownedAttribute>
        </packagedElement>
        <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:Class" xmi:id="cdif.UnitType" xmi:uuid="7f7cfbe5-b25e-5c58-94e3-5ab13e380d15">
