            <body>**CDIF**

Definition
==========

A Formal description of a set of values.</body>
            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdif.ValueAndConceptDescription"/>
          </ownedComment>
          <ownedAttribute xmi:type="uml:Property" xmi:id="cdif.ValueAndConceptDescription.cdi_classificationLevel" xmi:uuid="770ab8d0-002b-592b-a845-26b17190999f">
            <name>cdi:classificationLevel</name>
            <type xmi:type="uml:PrimitiveType" href="http://www.omg.org/spec/UML/20161101/PrimitiveTypes.xmi#String"/>
            <lowerValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger" xmi:id="cdif.ValueAndConceptDescription.cdi_classificationLevel.lower" xmi:uuid="d922fd01-d062-5db0-a9a7-1cdc43f0aaad">
              <value>0</value>
            </lowerValue>
            <upperValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural" xmi:id="cdif.ValueAndConceptDescription.cdi_classificationLevel.upper" xmi:uuid="949a97d4-1829-547c-bd23-cbf5d7283b76">
              <value>1</value>
            </upperValue>
            <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="cdif.ValueAndConceptDescription.cdi_classificationLevel.comment" xmi:uuid="bf7d1589-f3dd-59a2-a18d-bbc6ef09028a">
              <body>**CDIF**

Definition
==========

Indicates the type of relationship, nominal, ordinal, interval, ratio, or continuous. Use where appropriate for the representation type. type: Enumeration {Continuous, Interval, Nominal, Ordinal, Ratio}

**Original (DDICDI)**

*Definition:* Indicates the type of relationship, nominal, ordinal, interval, ratio, or continuous. Use where appropriate for the representation type.

`Specification item reference &lt;https://ddi-cdi.github.io/m2t-ng/DDI-CDI_1-1beta/field-level-documentation/DDICDILibrary/Classes/Representations/ValueAndConceptDescription.html&gt;`__</body>
              <annotatedElement xmi:idref="cdif.ValueAndConceptDescription.cdi_classificationLevel"/>
            </ownedComment>
          </ownedAttribute>
