        <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:Class" xmi:id="dcat.CatalogRecord" xmi:uuid="6c5506c0-4559-55a8-beec-f8426246589d">
          <name>CatalogRecord</name>
          <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="dcat.CatalogRecord.comment" xmi:uuid="d2c29dd3-2ef8-5b5b-abd5-d4ed59bfebe4">
            <body>**CDIF**

Definition
==========

This is the class used to provide information about the metadata record itself.

**Original (DCAT)**

*Definition:* A record in a data catalog, describing the registration of a single dataset or data service.

`Specification item reference &lt;http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#CatalogRecord&gt;`__</body>
            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="dcat.CatalogRecord"/>
          </ownedComment>
          <ownedAttribute xmi:type="uml:Property" xmi:id="dcat.CatalogRecord.conformsTo" xmi:uuid="9fe08e8e-1686-539d-b362-84f40b0aa0bb">
            <name>conformsTo</name>
            <type xmi:type="uml:PrimitiveType" href="http://www.omg.org/spec/UML/20161101/PrimitiveTypes.xmi#String"/>
            <lowerValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger" xmi:id="dcat.CatalogRecord.conformsTo.lower" xmi:uuid="c41365e1-ec19-50a9-b044-0b44210a519b">
              <value>1</value>
            </lowerValue>
            <upperValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural" xmi:id="dcat.CatalogRecord.conformsTo.upper" xmi:uuid="b2c802ae-1c38-5806-b41e-5ff14c4783dd">
              <value>*</value>
            </upperValue>
            <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="dcat.CatalogRecord.conformsTo.comment" xmi:uuid="fc1863ea-533e-570e-84de-0753f7ac2905">
              <body>**CDIF**

Definition
==========

Identifiers for conformance classes/profiles that the metadata record follows. For CDIF Core this must include 'https://w3id.org/cdif/core/1.1'; a record that also conforms to a higher-level profile (e.g. Discovery) lists that profile's identifier as well. | Identifiers for the conformance classes/profiles the metadata record follows. For the Data Structure profile this must include ``https://w3id.org/cdif/data_structure/1.1``. Records that also conform to Core, Discovery, Data Description (etc.) list those profile identifiers as well.</body>
              <annotatedElement xmi:idref="dcat.CatalogRecord.conformsTo"/>
            </ownedComment>
          </ownedAttribute>
