            <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="schema.DataDownload.DataDownload_cdif_coTypedAs_AbstractDataSet.comment" xmi:uuid="828998e2-51e6-5a78-a434-41ec7ed09383">
              <body>**CDIF**

Definition
==========

PROPOSED, not extracted: represents a DataDownload optionally being additionally co-typed as a TabularTextDataSet or StructuredDataSet, per config's own 'co-type a DataDownload may declare' framing - modeled as an association rather than a Generalization from DataDownload, since config's definition describes an orthogonal co-typing, not a further specialization within the existing AbstractDistribution branch.</body>
              <annotatedElement xmi:idref="schema.DataDownload.DataDownload_cdif_coTypedAs_AbstractDataSet"/>
            </ownedComment>
          </ownedAttribute>
        </packagedElement>
        <packagedElement xmi:type="uml:Class" xmi:id="schema.DefinedTerm" xmi:uuid="cef9b245-fe2b-5945-9b5f-a6e79c7b9103">
          <name>DefinedTerm</name>
          <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="schema.DefinedTerm.comment" xmi:uuid="4de34491-05b6-5ccf-ba9f-a247575f9a11">
            <body>**CDIF**

Definition
==========

*Authoritative definition: CDIF Core profile.*

**Original (Schema)**

*Definition:* A word, name, acronym, phrase, etc. with a formal definition. Often used in the context of category or subject classification, glossaries or dictionaries, product or creative work types, etc. Use the name property for the term being defined, use termCode if the term has an alpha-numeric code allocated, use description to provide the definition of the term. Use the about property to specify what the term is about.

`Specification item reference &lt;https://schema.org/DefinedTerm&gt;`__

:choiceConstraints:

- Required if absent: ``identifier``, ``termCode``
- Required if absent: ``name``, ``termCode``
- Required if absent: ``name``, ``identifier``</body>
            <annotatedElement xmi:idref="schema.DefinedTerm"/>
          </ownedComment>
          <generalization xmi:type="uml:Generalization" xmi:id="schema.DefinedTerm.gen.CdifConceptOrTerm" xmi:uuid="8ca52598-3488-5bc7-9a6c-ac86e978f6d5">
            <general xmi:idref="cdif.CdifConceptOrTerm"/>
          </generalization>
