            <name>identifier</name>
            <type xmi:idref="schema.Identifier"/>
            <lowerValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralInteger" xmi:id="schema.DefinedTerm.identifier.lower" xmi:uuid="5f1a03a9-5145-5522-9cef-28d27f7fd298">
              <value>0</value>
            </lowerValue>
            <upperValue xmi:type="uml:LiteralUnlimitedNatural" xmi:id="schema.DefinedTerm.identifier.upper" xmi:uuid="d556f1d9-389e-5d30-8b4e-8dab09ec8912">
              <value>1</value>
            </upperValue>
            <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="schema.DefinedTerm.identifier.comment" xmi:uuid="3803c2ae-edea-515a-86a8-c2e3828075c8">
              <body>**CDIF**

Definition
==========

string.uri or PropertyValue-(identifier) | string.uri or PropertyValue-(identifier)

**Original (Schema)**

*Definition:* The identifier property represents any kind of identifier for any kind of Thing, such as ISBNs, GTIN codes, UUIDs etc. Schema.org provides dedicated properties for representing many of these, either as textual strings or as URL (URI) links. See [background notes](/docs/datamodel.html#identifierBg) for more details.

`Specification item reference &lt;https://schema.org/identifier&gt;`__</body>
              <annotatedElement xmi:idref="schema.DefinedTerm.identifier"/>
            </ownedComment>
          </ownedAttribute>
        </packagedElement>
