              <body>**CDIF**

Definition
==========

Broader (parent) concepts. Any concept that is the target of ``skos:narrower`` on another concept must declare ``skos:broader`` pointing back. See Bidirectional hierarchy below. Each item is ``{"@id": "parent-concept-uri"}``.

**Original (SKOS)**

*Definition:* Relates a concept to a concept that is more general in meaning.

*Scope Note:* By convention, skos:broader is only used to assert an immediate (i.e. direct) hierarchical link between two conceptual resources.

`Specification item reference &lt;http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#broader&gt;`__</body>
              <annotatedElement xmi:idref="skos.Concept.broader"/>
            </ownedComment>
          </ownedAttribute>
