              <value>*</value>
            </upperValue>
            <ownedComment xmi:type="uml:Comment" xmi:id="skos.Concept.notation.comment" xmi:uuid="cbcde938-d43b-57c6-af2a-3d9cf127bf8e">
              <body>**CDIF**

Definition
==========

Classification codes. Should be unique within the scheme.

**Original (SKOS)**

*Definition:* A notation, also known as classification code, is a string of characters such as "T58.5" or "303.4833" used to uniquely identify a concept within the scope of a given concept scheme.

*Scope Note:* By convention, skos:notation is used with a typed literal in the object position of the triple.

`Specification item reference &lt;http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation&gt;`__</body>
              <annotatedElement xmi:idref="skos.Concept.notation"/>
            </ownedComment>
          </ownedAttribute>
